WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.279
For SSH or terminal users: add --terminal and --run to the same setup command.

00:00:08.279 --> 00:00:15.555
Choose a quantification matrix, raw DIA, raw DDA or an existing run. Enter accepts the displayed default.

00:00:15.555 --> 00:00:21.323
Provide the protein matrix and sample table. The same inputs work in browser setup.

00:00:21.323 --> 00:00:27.084
A matching FASTA can supply missing gene symbols. This synthetic table already includes gene names.

00:00:27.084 --> 00:00:34.356
Optionally add service quantification to benchmark shared proteins and detection gains or losses.

00:00:34.356 --> 00:00:40.120
Confirm independence only when samples represent different patients or biological replicates.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:48.902
Setup saves the configuration, reports the planned comparisons, and starts the real analysis.

00:00:48.902 --> 00:00:54.667
Later, from any working directory, continue by supplying the same project folder.

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:59.676
Setup saves the configuration, reports the planned comparisons, and starts the real analysis.

00:00:59.676 --> 00:01:06.192
Checksums and recorded inputs match. Completed results are reused without recomputation.

00:01:06.192 --> 00:01:13.201
Open START_HERE.html for results and MATRICES.html for clear CSV and TSV links.

